<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36435" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pīsistrătus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πεισίστρατος</span>.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pisistratus</i>, <i>tyrant of
			Athens</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 3, 33, 82</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Brut. 7,
				27</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Rep. 1, 44, 68</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. de
				Or. 3, 34, 137</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Ira, 3, 11, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 1, 2, 5</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pīsistrătĭdae</span></b> ,
				ārum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πεισιστρατίδαι</span>, <i>the
				Pisistratidœ</i>, i. e. <i>Hippias and
				Hipparchus</i>, <i>sons of Pisistratus</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 31,
				44, 8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A Bœotian chief</i>, <i>a
				friend of the Romans</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 33,
				27 sq.</span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
